  "youtube": {
    "description": "it's 2001. eighty thousand people screaming, one hairpin left and it's your race to lose. 🏁\nY2K drum & bass in the spirit of Rollcage Stage II and the PS1 racing era: breakbeats, rolling bass and that late 90s / early 2000s game soundtrack energy.\n\nPut it on for driving, gaming, coding, studying or just staring out the window pretending you're in a loading screen.\n\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\nTRACKLIST\n00:00 Checkered Stage\n01:55 Redline Protocol\n04:08 Turbo Circuit\n06:20 Fast Lap\n08:30 Hyper Podium\n10:39 Traction Drive\n12:51 Lost Paddock\n15:01 Velocity Protocol\n17:13 Victory Lane Transit\n19:26 Wheelspin Protocol\n21:37 Photo Finish Line\n23:48 Night Inertia\n25:58 Deep Burnout\n28:09 Slipstreamer Line\n30:21 Apex Transit\n32:31 Deep Gearshift\n34:43 Pit Lane Line\n36:53 Chicane Line\n39:04 Lost Hairpin\n41:14 Broken Grid\n43:24 Electric Grandstand\n45:35 Overtake Stage\n47:44 Last Lap Approach\n49:53 Pole Position Rush\n52:03 Electric Nitro\n54:12 Sector Three Line\n━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━\n\n🏎️ Visuals: Digital Aura Racing Team\n🎛️ Music: original tracks generated with custom Python scripts\n💿 Inspired by the sound of Rollcage Stage II and classic PS1 racers. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the original game or its publishers.\n\nIf this takes you back, drop your favourite old racing game in the comments and subscribe for more Y2K DnB.\n\n#y2kdnb #drumandbass #ps1",
